@baseUrl = https://localhost:7226

### Fetch a CSRF request token; keep the antiforgery cookie in the same client session.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/account/csrf

### Login requires the token from the response above in X-CSRF-TOKEN and its cookie.
### Supply your own confirmed, trusted-provisioned account and password locally; do not commit credentials.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/account/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: <token-from-csrf-response>

{
  "gymId": 1,
  "email": "member@example.com",
  "password": "<local-password>"
}

### Send the identity cookie obtained at login in the same client session.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/account/me
